# T07 trigger-started broadcast
# A P2P flow's send_done_trigger fires trigger 1; the broadcast has
# `trigger_bcast 1` as its start attribute, so all |G|-1 legs are
# attached to trigger 1 and launch together when it fires.
# Expect:
#   - one BCAST_COMPLETE with legs=6
#   - "Trigger 1 fired, 6 targets" (the synthetic trigger fires all
#      the legs of the broadcast, one target per leg)
Nodes 16
Grp 1 2 3 6 9 12 14
Connections 2
Triggers 1
5->10 id 1 start 0 size 4096 send_done_trigger 1
0->0 id 2 trigger_bcast 1 size 4096
trigger id 1 oneshot
